==== E. The walk: how many times it goes round, and which numbers of steps there are ====
divisors of 12 other than 1: [2, 3, 4, 6, 12]
   12 steps to a turn: a step is 1/12 of a turn = 1 hour-lengths of the clock; counting 0..11 and back to 0 goes round 1 time(s)
   6 steps to a turn: a step is 1/6 of a turn = 2 hour-lengths of the clock; counting 0..11 and back to 0 goes round 2 time(s)
   4 steps to a turn: a step is 1/4 of a turn = 3 hour-lengths of the clock; counting 0..11 and back to 0 goes round 3 time(s)
   3 steps to a turn: a step is 1/3 of a turn = 4 hour-lengths of the clock; counting 0..11 and back to 0 goes round 4 time(s)
   2 steps to a turn: a step is 1/2 of a turn = 6 hour-lengths of the clock; counting 0..11 and back to 0 goes round 6 time(s)
hour 6 at a quarter turn an hour: 1.5 turns

